{
 "$comment": "The guide's preferred spot (pos, face = a point she faces) and camera poses per room and device (pos = eye, look = orbit target, stand = the hotspot_N viewpoint of the stop; round 9: Step back returns to the start view), keyed by the tour artifact ids. Start views stand at the room's photograph viewpoint (assets-src/<room>/build_room.py CAMERAS: Muir cam_habs13, Albright cam_photo, Springfield cam_sc696, Robinson cam_ku1907, Lamarr cam_photo moved forward along its line of sight into the walkable street) at eye height 1.6 m. The guide's spot and the focus views were chosen by a search over the walkable floor (bounds.json) and the artifact nodes' boxes: on a 1440x900 desktop (fov 58) she is 33-52% of the screen height, on a 390x844 phone (fov 70) 24-42%; her head to waist is on screen and clear of the HUD (title plate, object list, hint, bubble; phone: everything below 590 px), she is seen from her front half, nothing stands between the eye and her chest, she does not cover a standing artifact, and the focused artifact is in frame beside her. Focus views look at most 8.5 degrees up (RoomControls focus mode clamps the polar angle at 0.55 pi). Round 5: Muir's mantel and pictures views face the fireplace wall (they had looked along it, edge-on); every focus is checked for path and framing by a script (yaw change, eye inside the room, artifact on screen and not edge-on). A pose may carry lookUp (degrees above the horizon its focus may look; RoomControls), for a subject high over the eye: the Hall of Fame tower and ball (Task 11 fix round 1). Round 8: the architecture-only stops were removed, and their poses with them; the labelled panel stops (Einstein's 1947 article, Naismith's uncle and McGill) stand on museum stands in front of the start view. Round 9 (owner feedback): the guide walks to another spot whenever the view settles where she would be out of frame, hidden or in front of the focus (room/RoomGuide.jsx, room/guideFrame.js); the focus views were searched again for the records that moved onto walls, easels near the architecture and stages (each record face-on, nothing between it and the eye, a spot for the guide beside it: e2e/camcheck.mjs and e2e/chapters.mjs --only=guide check every one), and a focus view may stand on rising ground (North Hall's lawn: its eye 1.6 m above the ground there).",
